{"fileId":"1XW053aQeCA4ikZO0RhgZrFom57UqD7m0","sourceSha256":"2ede6fff852fa7e2d0363be49f58bc9522fac3209e335e6c03b007f916568780","blocks":{"4551d4789ecfe425fdf1":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"A modal is a type of auxiliary (helping) verb that is used to ex- press: permission, prohibition or obligation. ➢ Permission – can, may, could","bbox":[91.42500305175781,427.1960144042969,502.0817565917969,467.8000183105469]},"cd857324426a753b0ed8":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"'Can' is most often used to ask for or give permission but 'may' and 'could' are also possible even though they are not used as often as 'can'. • Can I wash my hands? • You can use this hand sanitizer if you don’t have soap","bbox":[127.44999694824219,467.9960021972656,525.8099975585938,542.0299682617188]},"90c494c0dd4b5ac06400":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"with you. • Could I use the computer to research more about CoVID-19? • May I get some updates about CoVID-19 cases here in Muntinlupa?","bbox":[163.4499969482422,542.4259643554688,524.010009765625,602.2300415039062]},"dccb616af706839611f2":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"➢ Prohibition 'Can't' and 'mustn't' (must not) are used to show that some- thing is prohibited (not allowed)","bbox":[109.44999694824219,603.2459716796875,478.9776306152344,642.25]},"5218c120444040d1e371":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"• You can't go outside the house without your mask on. • You mustn't touch your face especially your eyes, mouth and nose.","bbox":[145.4499969482422,641.6900024414062,526.8099975585938,687.4500122070312]},"37bf05f3785445a574ca":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"➢ Obligation 'Have to' and 'must' are both used to express obligation. There is a slight difference in the way that they are both used. 'Have to' shows that the obligation comes from someone else, not the speaker. This is usually referring to a rule or law.","bbox":[109.44999694824219,688.4459838867188,525.513916015625,752.4750366210938]},"39aed6250245f1f64167":{"type":"paragraph","page":5,"text":"• We have to stay at home to prevent getting exposed to the virus. People have to maintain physical distance to prevent the spread of CoVID-19. • The frontliners have to wear personal protective equip- ment to protect themselves from getting infected.","bbox":[145.4499969482422,70.77001953125,511.2200012207031,135.3199920654297]},"66f042e223bcdb6d6c6f":{"type":"paragraph","page":5,"text":"➢ Here is an example of the difference between 'have to' and 'must':","bbox":[109.44999694824219,149.11598205566406,535.0400390625,163.11997985839844]},"bb1159a9e1cf1a5ee58c":{"type":"paragraph","page":5,"text":"• My doctor said that I have to get myself tested for CoVID-19 or I'll risk serious problems. (I have no choice) • I must get myself tested for CoVID-19 so that I’d be sure. (it’s my decision)","bbox":[145.4499969482422,175.78997802734375,496.82000732421875,227.9499969482422]},"a568e3d9035f906194a4":{"type":"paragraph","page":5,"text":"➢ We use 'don't have to' to show that there is no obligation. You can do something if you want but it is not an obligation.","bbox":[87.625,253.3460235595703,534.0059814453125,279.98004150390625]},"67c993209d755f3f6fa4":{"type":"paragraph","page":5,"text":"• You don't have to help everyone but it would be nice to help a person and show our support with each other in the midst of this pandemic. • Students don't have to be at risk to acquire education, teachers are doing their best to equip themselves to deliver education in their stu- dents’ homes.","bbox":[123.6500015258789,291.010009765625,545.6296997070312,355.3700256347656]},"17dfbdd07d6d0f163f7f":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"This module was designed and written with you in mind. It is here to","bbox":[108.05000305175781,149.09243774414062,535.0480346679688,163.1256103515625]},"d2045914be2ff9587e3e":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"help you express permission, obligation, and prohibition using modals. The scope of this module permits it to be used in many different learning situations. The language used recognizes the diverse vocabulary level of students.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,163.14601135253906,535.0400390625,205.3500213623047]},"d78179f71230b38c0b48":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"After going through this module, you are expected to:","bbox":[108.05000305175781,205.3460235595703,424.7900085449219,219.3500213623047]},"c9253b39cbbf65c0328e":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"Define modal; Recognize modals in sentences; Identify the function expressed by modal verbs (permission, obligation, and prohibition) in sample sentences; and Write sentences granting permission, declaring obligation, or announcing prohibition using appropriate modals.","bbox":[144.0500030517578,219.5459747314453,535.0400390625,303.98004150390625]},"da320112b816a54d43a2":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"Directions: Choose the letter of the best answer. Use a separate sheet of paper for your answers. 1. Which of the following is used to express obligation?","bbox":[90.0250015258789,429.3960266113281,506.50146484375,471.6000061035156]},"d1402e7d6d1710018302":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"A. can","bbox":[128.85000610351562,471.59600830078125,169.489990234375,485.6000061035156]},"c55aed0d3987fb6d8382":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"C. must","bbox":[306.1000061035156,471.59600830078125,356.55999755859375,485.6000061035156]},"dda12b21e7ae5cb6b51e":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"B. may","bbox":[126.05000305175781,485.7960205078125,169.69000244140625,499.8000183105469]},"569a525f1c859c46856c":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"D. must not","bbox":[306.1000061035156,485.7960205078125,380.3699951171875,499.8000183105469]},"bf96c5db2d8a337f3192":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"2. The following words are used to express permission, EXCEPT ONE: A. can","bbox":[108.05000305175781,514.0259399414062,528.6400146484375,542.0299682617188]},"5177ec5a6a5e2c981f74":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"C. have to","bbox":[306.1000061035156,528.0259399414062,368.9700012207031,542.0299682617188]},"dc179bcbad3e319f702c":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"B. could","bbox":[126.05000305175781,542.2260131835938,177.11000061035156,556.2300415039062]},"482ddf9efe6f69ca67e5":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"D. may","bbox":[306.1000061035156,542.2260131835938,351.760009765625,556.2300415039062]},"453f2abeff415869cf51":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"3. Prohibition is expressed by using the words A. can & may C. must & mustn’t B. could & must","bbox":[108.05000305175781,570.2260131835938,431.989990234375,612.4199829101562]},"81e59610974c5040c48f":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"D. mustn’t & can’t","bbox":[306.1000061035156,598.4159545898438,430.5899963378906,612.4199829101562]},"efba862b20bbac3f809a":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"is a type of auxiliary verb that is used","bbox":[213.67999267578125,626.64599609375,438.7900085449219,640.6500244140625]},"a48ae7d3754ebb6ea3a9":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"to express: permission, prohibition, and obligation. A. Action verb","bbox":[126.05000305175781,640.8460083007812,429.19000244140625,668.8500366210938]},"b83c1524ff671d081b21":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"C. Stative verb","bbox":[306.1000061035156,654.8460083007812,399.989990234375,668.8500366210938]},"d9736bc85ba88c555d57":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"B. Modal verb","bbox":[126.05000305175781,668.8460083007812,209.11000061035156,682.8500366210938]},"ec3c5c1e239a9b718870":{"type":"paragraph","page":2,"text":"D. Transitive verb","bbox":[306.1000061035156,668.8460083007812,414.19000244140625,682.8500366210938]},"1129b12ca0c50fef6d3d":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"5. Health is at risk because of CoViD-19: therefore, we have to take good care of our well-being and follow the health proto- cols that implemented. Which is the modal in the sentence? A. at risk","bbox":[108.05000305175781,71.91596984863281,480.2200012207031,128.11997985839844]},"2b10c0212a1dd75c4732":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"C. health protocols","bbox":[306.1000061035156,114.11598205566406,420.989990234375,128.11997985839844]},"84b684d329c06072a705":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"B. have to","bbox":[128.64999389648438,128.3159942626953,190.3199920654297,142.3199920654297]},"1cf6235f21957dc1420a":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"D. well-being","bbox":[288.1000061035156,128.3159942626953,387.7900085449219,142.3199920654297]},"51ebfbeae6a0eb483dc0":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"For items 6-10 Directions: Identify the function expressed in the following sentences. Choose from the choices below.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,170.5459747314453,535.0400390625,212.74998474121094]},"e40098b7ae26c21b9ac6":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"A. Obligation","bbox":[180.0800018310547,226.9459991455078,260.3399963378906,240.9499969482422]},"245019786ab3df99dc40":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"C. Prohibition","bbox":[324.1300048828125,226.9459991455078,409.3899841308594,240.9499969482422]},"8bd7e72413c8aa4b8cb2":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"B. Permission","bbox":[180.0800018310547,240.9459991455078,265.1399841308594,254.9499969482422]},"02aeda6f77252b456c4c":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"D. Suggestion","bbox":[324.1300048828125,240.9459991455078,409.5899963378906,254.9499969482422]},"71253eaacf46f5946944":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"6. Muntinlupeños have to follow CoViD-19 protocols all the time to help main- tain the peace and order in the city while the front liners and the local gov- ernment try to eradicate the spread of the disease. 7. During the CoViD-19 pandemic, the front liners are doing their part in sav- ing lives and promoting health. We must do our part as well by staying at home and keeping ourselves healthy. 8. The proliferation of fake news about CoViD-19 today may cause fear and panic. 9. We can stop CoViD-19 from spreading by being updated, staying at home and keeping ourselves healthy. 10. The elderly, children and pregnant women must not go outside for they are more susceptible to infections.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,269.1659851074219,535.0400390625,438.20001220703125]},"4f71831fb79e2c77e1e7":{"type":"figure","page":3,"bbox":[72.0,447.4300231933594,263.91998291015625,530.530029296875],"src":"/assets/curriculum/figures/329cf4ac05a4e7f255a4c3d7.webp","width":488,"height":185,"monochrome":true},"6b36517d5a337ff82209":{"type":"paragraph","page":3,"text":"Directions: Give the function expressed by each of the underlined sentences and the word that helped you identify it. Write your an- swers in the table that follows.","bbox":[100.43000030517578,539.6160278320312,506.8077087402344,579.8200073242188]},"a91e64faeef991eefa18":{"type":"diagram","bbox":[97.0,586.5399780273438,510.25,706.5399780273438],"width":413.25,"height":120.0,"shapes":[{"d":"M0.00,0.00 h413.25 v120.00 h-413.25 Z","stroke":"#000000","fill":"none","width":2.25},{"d":"M44.45,14.98 h361.33 v0.60 h-361.33 Z","stroke":"none","fill":"#000000","width":1},{"d":"M8.45,27.41 h56.20 v0.60 h-56.20 Z","stroke":"none","fill":"#000000","width":1},{"d":"M353.15,39.81 h52.62 v0.60 h-52.62 Z","stroke":"none","fill":"#000000","width":1},{"d":"M8.45,52.21 h247.27 v0.60 h-247.27 Z","stroke":"none","fill":"#000000","width":1},{"d":"M258.93,52.21 h146.85 v0.60 h-146.85 Z","stroke":"none","fill":"#000000","width":1},{"d":"M8.45,64.61 h184.65 v0.60 h-184.65 Z","stroke":"none","fill":"#000000","width":1},{"d":"M247.33,77.01 h158.45 v0.60 h-158.45 Z","stroke":"none","fill":"#000000","width":1},{"d":"M8.45,89.41 h123.83 v0.60 h-123.83 Z","stroke":"none","fill":"#000000","width":1},{"d":"M135.88,89.41 h269.90 v0.60 h-269.90 Z","stroke":"none","fill":"#000000","width":1},{"d":"M8.45,101.81 h85.03 v0.60 h-85.03 Z","stroke":"none","fill":"#000000","width":1}],"labels":[{"text":"You must protect yourself and those people around you from ","x":44.45,"y":13.58,"size":11.0},{"text":"CoVID-19. Taking appropriate precautions will help you avoid getting in-","x":8.45,"y":26.01,"size":11.0},{"text":"fected by the virus. Some are the common ways to prevent it: First, you ","x":8.45,"y":38.41,"size":11.0},{"text":"must not touch your face especially your eyes, mouth or nose. You have to ","x":8.45,"y":50.81,"size":11.0},{"text":"wash your hands with soap often. Stay at home and don’t go outside if it ","x":8.45,"y":63.21,"size":11.0},{"text":"is not necessary or if you’re not feeling well. In case you miss your friends ","x":8.45,"y":75.61,"size":11.0},{"text":"or loved ones, you may still connect with them through calls or any social ","x":8.45,"y":88.01,"size":11.0},{"text":"media platform. With these, you won’t risk your health or your loved ones. ","x":8.45,"y":100.41,"size":11.0}],"text":"You must protect yourself and those people around you from  CoVID-19. Taking appropriate precautions will help you avoid getting in- fected by the virus. Some are the common ways to prevent it: First, you  must not touch your face especially your eyes, mouth or nose. You have to  wash your hands with soap often. Stay at home and don’t go outside if it  is not necessary or if you’re not feeling well. In case you miss your friends  or loved ones, you may still connect with them through calls or any social  media platform. With these, you won’t risk your health or your loved ones. ","page":3},"06e5c3594946dd0cbac9":{"type":"heading","page":4,"text":"FUNCTION","bbox":[353.92999267578125,85.85797119140625,418.69000244140625,98.6729736328125]},"016172610f3ed081823b":{"type":"heading","page":4,"text":"SENTENCE","bbox":[157.0500030517578,92.25799560546875,224.02000427246094,105.072998046875]},"f024ce6e003e9b564a3f":{"type":"heading","page":4,"text":"WORD CLUE","bbox":[467.5799865722656,92.25799560546875,542.5399780273438,105.072998046875]},"f81ecb0dcd37ededc96e":{"type":"heading","page":4,"text":"EXPRESSED","bbox":[345.9200134277344,99.0579833984375,420.8899841308594,111.87298583984375]},"0b98638e40afa9d41fe6":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"You must protect yourself and those people around you from CoVID-19. First, you must not touch your face, es- pecially","bbox":[79.625,115.468017578125,293.5419921875,166.30502319335938]},"a0727baf199737472f7b":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"your","bbox":[147.4499969482422,153.468017578125,175.37001037597656,166.30502319335938]},"27f73d364a85bda9b4a8":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"eyes,","bbox":[185.27000427246094,153.468017578125,215.40000915527344,166.30502319335938]},"ef645d5326bba9faa11e":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"mouth","bbox":[225.67999267578125,153.468017578125,264.6199951171875,166.30502319335938]},"6c115c2af0af92c9d13e":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"and","bbox":[275.5,153.468017578125,298.6199951171875,166.30502319335938]},"4ae38536cb973b6f5300":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"nose. You have to wash your hands with soap often. In case you miss your friends or loved ones, you may still connect with them through calls or any social media platform.","bbox":[79.625,166.28802490234375,301.4730529785156,257.3249816894531]},"113dbd182c33318feafb":{"type":"paragraph","page":4,"text":"Modal Verbs","bbox":[260.8999938964844,400.3960266113281,341.40997314453125,414.46002197265625]},"87545d24e67018be4f18":{"type":"paragraph","page":6,"text":"Directions: Use modals in writing sentences that express what people can do, should not do, and must do to help fight the spread of CoVID-","bbox":[90.0250015258789,452.7960205078125,507.0115661621094,480.20001220703125]},"fc4cf7ddd3583d5d5fa4":{"type":"heading","page":6,"text":"PERMISSION","bbox":[275.5,520.8159790039062,356.5999755859375,534.7960205078125]},"170e47b65762773cc86b":{"type":"heading","page":6,"text":"PROHIBITION","bbox":[268.5,621.2459716796875,359.2099914550781,635.2260131835938]},"c73411d961f9d25458b5":{"type":"heading","page":7,"text":"OBLIGATION","bbox":[271.8999938964844,106.91596984863281,356.3999938964844,120.8959732055664]},"ce3774fc204cf5c07411":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"A modal is a type of auxiliary (helping) verb that is used to ex- press: permission, prohibition or obligation. ➢ Permission – can, may, could","bbox":[101.0199966430664,387.9960021972656,487.85174560546875,427.6000061035156]},"c3bae9a21dbbf13c40b0":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"'Can' is most often used to ask for or give permission but 'may' and 'could' are also possible even though they are not used as often as 'can'. ➢ Prohibition 'Can't' and 'mustn't' (must not) are used to show that something is prohibited (not allowed) ➢ Obligation 'Have to' and 'must' are both used to express obligation. There is a slight difference in the way that they are both used. 'Have to' shows that the obligation comes from someone else, not the speaker. This is usually referring to a rule or law.","bbox":[137.0500030517578,427.7960205078125,546.0399780273438,582.6200561523438]},"79f4a08b228b9bc81fc2":{"type":"paragraph","page":7,"text":"Directions: Write an argumentative paragraph on the given topic. Use modals to express permission, obligation, and prohibition.","bbox":[90.0250015258789,736.27099609375,520.3296508789062,763.875]},"bad4073c9618ec208897":{"type":"heading","page":8,"text":"Should curfew be imposed further as an intervention to stop the spread of","bbox":[64.2249984741211,88.52601623535156,532.6799926757812,102.50601959228516]},"9e174ea841a8ded22ec2":{"type":"heading","page":8,"text":"CoViD-19?","bbox":[263.1000061035156,102.72602844238281,334.0,116.7060317993164]},"f9ace5c7eb260780c497":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"Directions: Choose the correct modal from the box to complete the sen- tences.","bbox":[72.0250015258789,382.59600830078125,495.48565673828125,410.6000061035156]},"2a7286ea81c90f595e1a":{"type":"heading","page":8,"text":"can’t","bbox":[90.625,420.7960205078125,126.1300048828125,434.7760009765625]},"cd898cf7dbc06aefd12e":{"type":"heading","page":8,"text":"can","bbox":[162.64999389648438,420.7960205078125,188.75,434.7760009765625]},"994c11217c066913a06a":{"type":"heading","page":8,"text":"may","bbox":[234.8800048828125,420.7960205078125,265.3799743652344,434.7760009765625]},"4233d7b5c6a2673e5bba":{"type":"heading","page":8,"text":"must not","bbox":[306.8999938964844,420.7960205078125,367.79998779296875,434.7760009765625]},"70f588b98059ed42c053":{"type":"heading","page":8,"text":"must","bbox":[414.95001220703125,420.7960205078125,450.6299743652344,434.7760009765625]},"a8a1a778cd693ae7a273":{"type":"heading","page":8,"text":"have to","bbox":[486.9800109863281,420.7960205078125,537.280029296875,434.7760009765625]},"0d16a66a969a8ba0fca9":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"1. You _________spread fake news on CoViD-19 in your social media account. You are putting lives at risk!","bbox":[100.43000030517578,457.3960266113281,517.2200317382812,485.4000244140625]},"f79a701fad86a94c3368":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"2. Police and health workers _________ wear masks while on duty to prevent getting infected.","bbox":[100.43000030517578,497.61602783203125,517.2200317382812,525.6200561523438]},"23df4df486577a15217f":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"3. Other than the front liners, other people _________ help fight the spread of the virus by staying at home.","bbox":[100.43000030517578,537.6160278320312,517.2200317382812,565.8200073242188]},"d64e42e5784c65276b85":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"4. You don’t ________ go outside to buy food because the local govern- ment units are ready to provide you with it.","bbox":[100.43000030517578,577.8159790039062,513.3639526367188,606.030029296875]},"4beb200ebc619b538027":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"5. People _________ attend mass gatherings to prevent the spread of the virus, but, they can be connected with everybody by the use of var- ious mediums such as phone call, video call and online chat among others.","bbox":[100.43000030517578,618.0459594726562,517.2200317382812,674.25]},"e4791ce18d9c9e2c593a":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"6. We ________ flatten the curve of CoVID-19 to reduce further damage it may cause us.","bbox":[100.43000030517578,686.4459838867188,517.2200317382812,714.4500122070312]},"7ea506c77ae9e254b9be":{"type":"paragraph","page":8,"text":"7-8. You ________ be updated in the events that are happening around us because this ________ help us in making ourselves safe.","bbox":[100.43000030517578,726.6659545898438,517.2200317382812,754.6749877929688]},"4d66aac4fe21541a7232":{"type":"paragraph","page":9,"text":"9. CoVID-19 _________ greatly affect our economy because it disrupts businesses, the supply of goods and others.","bbox":[100.43000030517578,71.91596984863281,517.2200317382812,99.91996765136719]},"b45692bff0f5d04bdf25":{"type":"paragraph","page":9,"text":"10. During the quarantine, people _________ go to non-essential places to avoid the risk of contracting the disease.","bbox":[100.43000030517578,112.11598205566406,517.2200317382812,140.11997985839844]},"c4dfb36100d71e031a4e":{"type":"paragraph","page":10,"text":"Must not","bbox":[310.6600036621094,191.09999084472656,363.82000732421875,205.10398864746094]},"5b15bc6722a1c3ea54ed":{"type":"figure","page":10,"bbox":[98.95001220703125,194.25,260.3500061035156,444.6499938964844],"src":"/assets/curriculum/figures/c95461e5d5ce01e02e522b77.webp","width":448,"height":695,"monochrome":true},"09eae0e629a747851dab":{"type":"figure","page":10,"bbox":[267.70001220703125,194.15000915527344,442.8999938964844,441.95001220703125],"src":"/assets/curriculum/figures/8048a437e2f9e7a91997f1e7.webp","width":486,"height":688,"monochrome":true},"329d953505c25849f11c":{"type":"paragraph","page":10,"text":"9. Can","bbox":[363.989990234375,214.50001525878906,409.6499938964844,228.50401306152344]},"1eedd99cc490a7ac4cc2":{"type":"paragraph","page":10,"text":"B","bbox":[196.19000244140625,230.8000030517578,208.8300018310547,244.8040008544922]},"e4acc3bd0714bd7a5c4e":{"type":"paragraph","page":10,"text":